==================================================
BACKGROUND
==================================================

The application is an existing DevOps Automation Console running on a VM.

It already has:
- FastAPI backend
- Existing Kubernetes authentication/session management
- Kubernetes Python client integration
- Existing Kubernetes pod discovery
- Existing pod metrics functionality
- Pod status/restart/CPU/memory/replica information
- Existing WebSocket/session infrastructure
- Existing Pega-specific Log Streamer
- Existing log viewer/terminal UI
- Existing Kibana-style log processing/filtering/error grouping functionality in the Pega log streamer

The existing Pega Log Streamer is application-specific.

Pega logs are written to a NAS mounted to both the Kubernetes environment and the VM. The existing Pega streamer reads those files from the VM and streams them to the UI.

We now need a SECOND, GENERIC log streamer for other Kubernetes applications that do not have centralized observability/logging infrastructure.

The new streamer must obtain logs directly from Kubernetes using the existing Kubernetes Python client/session/authentication infrastructure.

Do NOT introduce:
- Elasticsearch
- OpenSearch
- Kibana server
- Kafka
- Loki
- Fluent Bit
- OpenTelemetry
- another logging database
- permanent log storage

The purpose is a lightweight operational troubleshooting utility.

==================================================
IMPORTANT ARCHITECTURAL PRINCIPLE
==================================================

There must be TWO independent log-streamer modules.

1. Pega Log Streamer
   - Existing functionality
   - Pega/NAS-specific
   - Currently tied to application 55042
   - Must remain functionally unchanged
   - Must be renamed/reorganized explicitly as "Pega Log Streamer"

2. Kubernetes Log Streamer
   - New generic implementation
   - Uses Kubernetes Python client
   - Discovers Kubernetes pods
   - Retrieves historical pod/container logs
   - Optionally follows live logs
   - Uses temporary disk-backed session workspaces
   - Must NOT depend on the Pega implementation

Do NOT convert the existing Pega streamer into a generic abstraction as part of this work.

Do NOT share the Pega log-processing implementation directly with the new streamer.

The new implementation should independently reproduce the useful log-viewer capabilities that already exist in the Pega streamer.

Shared infrastructure such as authentication/session management may be reused where appropriate.

